\name{cellucid_field_push}
\alias{cellucid_field_push}
\title{Add a column of values}
\usage{
cellucid_field_push(viewer, key, kind, categories, n_obs, cells, values)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{key}{The column's name. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}
\item{kind}{One of \code{"categorical"}, \code{"continuous"}. Required.}
\item{categories}{A categorical column's categories (its values are codes into them; the largest code is "no category"); null for a continuous one. A vector or list of text or \code{NULL}. Required.}
\item{n_obs}{The cells of the dataset the column belongs to. A whole number (at least 0). Required.}
\item{cells}{Cells: 1-based positions, \code{TRUE}/\code{FALSE} for every cell, or the cell names of the object the viewer shows, each once (sent as original positions). Required.}
\item{values}{One value per cell named: a code (categorical) or a number (continuous). A column, one value per cell named: numbers (\code{NA}: no value), or a factor (its codes; \code{NA}: no category). Required.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
A notebook's column as a field of the cells: categorical (codes into its categories) or continuous; a later push of the same name replaces it.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{field.push} (Fields). It changes the viewer's state: one step of the viewer's history, labelled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{field-overlays}, \code{active-field}, \code{filters}, \code{colors}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_field_push(viewer, categories = list(),
      cells = integer(0), key = "x", kind = "categorical",
      n_obs = 0, values = numeric(0))
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
